int \fBmb_set_debug_records\fP(
 		int \fIverbose\fP,
 		void \fI*mbio_ptr\fP,
 		bool \fIenable_debug_record_type_listing\fP,
 		int \fInum_debug_record_identifiers\fP,
 		mb_name \fI*debug_record_identifiers\fP,
 		int \fI*error\fP);

The function \fBmb_set_debug_records\fP configures the \fBMBIO\fP
descriptor pointed to by \fImbio_ptr\fP to print a debug listing
of selected data record types as they are read. If
\fIenable_debug_record_type_listing\fP is true, the
\fInum_debug_record_identifiers\fP record type names in the array
\fIdebug_record_identifiers\fP are the ones listed; this is a
debugging aid for programs (e.g. \fBmbtrnpp\fP) that process
streamed input.

\---------------------------------------------------------
.br
int \fBmb_set_platform\fP(
 		int \fIverbose\fP,
 		void \fI*mbio_ptr\fP,
 		void \fI*mbplatform_ptr\fP,
 		int \fI*error\fP);

The function \fBmb_set_platform\fP attaches a previously
initialized sensor platform model (see \fBmb_platform_init\fP)
pointed to by \fImbplatform_ptr\fP to the \fBMBIO\fP descriptor
pointed to by \fImbio_ptr\fP, so that subsequent reads through
that descriptor can make use of the platform's sensor offsets.

