int \fBmb_extract_platform\fP(
 		int \fIverbose\fP,
 		void \fI*mbio_ptr\fP,
 		void \fI*store_ptr\fP,
 		int \fI*kind\fP,
 		void \fI**platform_ptr\fP,
 		int \fI*error\fP);

The function \fBmb_extract_platform\fP extracts sensor platform
information (the sonar and auxiliary sensor positions and
orientation offsets) embedded in the current data record, where
the data format supports this, and returns it as a newly
allocated platform structure pointed to by \fI*platform_ptr\fP
(see \fBmb_platform_init\fP below). This is used by
\fBmb_preprocess\fP when a per-file or per-record platform
definition is available directly from the raw data rather than
from a separately supplied platform file.

