.br
int \fBmb_sensorhead\fP(
 		int \fIverbose\fP,
 		void \fI*mbio_ptr\fP,
 		void \fI*store_ptr\fP,
 		int \fI*sensorhead\fP,
 		int \fI*error\fP);

The function \fBmb_sensorhead\fP returns the index of the sensor
head (transducer) that produced the current data record, for
multi-head sonar systems (e.g. the Kraken/RESON WISSL laser
system) where the data format distinguishes among heads.

\---------------------------------------------------------
.br
int \fBmb_preprocess\fP(
 		int \fIverbose\fP,
 		void \fI*mbio_ptr\fP,
 		void \fI*store_ptr\fP,
 		void \fI*platform_ptr\fP,
 		void \fI*preprocess_pars_ptr\fP,
 		int \fI*error\fP);

The function \fBmb_preprocess\fP applies sensor offset, timing,
and navigation/attitude merging corrections to the current data
record read by \fImbio_ptr\fP, using the platform model pointed
to by \fIplatform_ptr\fP (see \fBmb_platform_init\fP) and the
options and merge navigation/attitude time series pointed to by
\fIpreprocess_pars_ptr\fP (a \fIstruct mb_preprocess_struct\fP,
filled in by the calling program, typically \fBmbpreprocess\fP).
If the data format has registered its own preprocessing routine,
that routine is called; otherwise \fBmb_preprocess_generic\fP is
called so that platform-based preprocessing is available for
every supported data format.

\---------------------------------------------------------
.br
int \fBmb_preprocess_generic\fP(
 		int \fIverbose\fP,
 		void \fI*mbio_ptr\fP,
 		void \fI*store_ptr\fP,
 		void \fI*platform_ptr\fP,
 		void \fI*preprocess_pars_ptr\fP,
 		int \fI*error\fP);

The function \fBmb_preprocess_generic\fP implements the
format-independent (generic) version of the preprocessing
corrections applied by \fBmb_preprocess\fP, operating solely
through the standard \fBMBIO\fP \fBmb_extract\fP/\fBmb_insert\fP
family of functions. It is used automatically by
\fBmb_preprocess\fP for any data format that has not registered a
format-specific preprocessing routine of its own.

