.br
int \fBmb_loadnavdata\fP(
 		int \fIverbose\fP,
 		char \fI*merge_nav_file\fP,
 		int \fImerge_nav_format\fP,
 		int \fImerge_nav_lonflip\fP,
 		int \fI*merge_nav_num\fP,
 		int \fI*merge_nav_alloc\fP,
 		double \fI**merge_nav_time_d\fP,
 		double \fI**merge_nav_lon\fP,
 		double \fI**merge_nav_lat\fP,
 		double \fI**merge_nav_speed\fP,
 		int \fI*error\fP);

The function \fBmb_loadnavdata\fP reads an entire external
navigation file \fImerge_nav_file\fP (of \fBMBIO\fP format
\fImerge_nav_format\fP, applying \fImerge_nav_lonflip\fP) into
time, longitude, latitude, and speed arrays that are allocated (or
reallocated, tracked by \fI*merge_nav_alloc\fP) and returned as
\fI*merge_nav_time_d\fP, \fI*merge_nav_lon\fP, \fI*merge_nav_lat\fP,
and \fI*merge_nav_speed\fP, with \fI*merge_nav_num\fP set to the
number of values read. This is used by programs such as
\fBmbprocess\fP to merge externally logged navigation into swath
data using \fBmb_linear_interp\fP or \fBmb_linear_interp_longitude\fP
and \fBmb_linear_interp_latitude\fP.

