 		int \fIverbose\fP,
 		void \fI*modelptr\fP,
 		double \fIsource_depth\fP,
 		double \fIsource_angle\fP,
 		double \fIend_time\fP,
 		int \fIssv_mode\fP,
 		double \fIsurface_vel\fP,
 		double \fInull_angle\fP,
 		int \fInplot_max\fP,
 		int \fI*nplot\fP,
 		double \fI*xplot\fP,
 		double \fI*zplot\fP,
 		double \fI*tplot\fP,
 		double \fI*x\fP,
 		double \fI*z\fP,
 		double \fI*travel_time\fP,
 		int \fI*ray_stat\fP,
 		int \fI*error\fP);

The function \fBmb_rt\fP traces a single ray, launched from
\fIsource_depth\fP at takeoff angle \fIsource_angle\fP, through
the layered velocity model \fImodelptr\fP (initialized by
\fBmb_rt_init\fP) until either the elapsed travel time reaches
\fIend_time\fP or the ray exits the model (surfacing, in which case
\fIssv_mode\fP and \fIsurface_vel\fP control how the ray reflects
off the sea surface, and rays arriving within \fInull_angle\fP of
vertical are treated specially). The ray path is returned as up to
\fInplot_max\fP plotting points in \fIxplot\fP/\fIzplot\fP/\fItplot\fP
(with the actual number of points returned in \fI*nplot\fP), and
